@startuml recovery-workflow
!include plantuml-style.puml
title Pi-rendered recovery card and manual NFC read-back
hide footbox

actor User
participant "Rust CLI" as CLI
participant "Pi laser API" as API
participant "Operator browser" as Browser
participant "Phone: QRbot / NFC Tools" as Phone
participant "Wooden NTAG215 card" as Card
participant "Opaque RF-shielded holder" as Holder
participant Service

User -> Service: Save recovery codes
activate Service
deactivate Service
User -> CLI: submit: JSON job + codes-only UTF-8 file
CLI -> API: POST /api/jobs/review
API -> API: Encode QR, render fonts and separate side rasters
API --> CLI: Review ID; no laser start
note over CLI, API
The CLI has no PDF, QR, image or font renderer.
Keep login passwords separate from recovery codes.
Start with fictional data; neither QR nor NFC is encryption.
end note
User -> Browser: Inspect exact front and back previews
User -> Browser: Confirm placement; start front
Browser -> API: Plan and run front (explicit operator action)
API --> Browser: Software outcome, not physical acceptance
User -> Browser: Confirm rest, inspect front, record verdict
User -> User: Flip and seat card in the same guide
User -> Browser: Confirm placement; start back separately
Browser -> API: Plan and run back (separate operator action)
API --> Browser: Software outcome
User -> Browser: Confirm rest, inspect back, record verdict
User -> Phone: Scan finished QR; compare source payload
User -> User: Prepare and secure an independent paper backup
note over Phone, Card
Manual NFC Tools workflow, not a CLI or Pi NFC adapter.
Check tag compatibility and full NDEF storage first.
Optional tag read protection cannot protect the QR.
Do not expose an antenna or chip to the laser.
end note
User -> Phone: Explicitly choose one English NDEF Text record
Phone -> Card: Write payload
Card --> Phone: Read full text back
User -> User: Compare complete payload with source
User -> Holder: Store card; secure paper separately
User -> Phone: Clear temporary copies and history

group Recovery after successful backup
    note over User, Holder
If the card is unavailable, use the separate paper backup.
After loss or suspected copying, replace the code set
and every backup. A spare copy does not revoke a lost one.
end note
    User -> Holder: Remove card
    activate Phone
    alt NFC
        Phone -> Card: Read with NFC Tools
        activate Card
        Card --> Phone: Codes and instructions
        deactivate Card
    else QR
        User -> Phone: Scan with QRbot; view text
    end
    Phone --> User: Display codes and instructions
    deactivate Phone
    User -> Service: Follow instructions; use one unused code
    activate Service
    deactivate Service
    User -> User: Mark code spent with marker; clear temporary copies; store card
end
@enduml